# Development Workflow and Best Practices

## Virtual Environment
- **ALWAYS** use the virtual environment (venv) for Python dependencies
- Activate venv before running any Python-related commands
- Use `.venv` or `venv` directory in the project root
- Never install or run Python packages without virtual environment

## Development Commands
- `npm run dev` - Start development server (port 3000)
- `npm run build` - Create production build
- Use `npm install` for adding new dependencies
- Use `npm update` for updating existing dependencies

## Code Quality
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Implement proper error handling
- Write clean, readable code with proper comments
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Follow the established project structure

## Testing and Debugging
- Use browser dev tools for debugging
- Implement proper console logging for development
- Test on multiple devices and browsers
- Use React DevTools for component debugging
- Test Persian/Farsi text rendering

## Git Workflow
- Use meaningful commit messages
- Create feature branches for new features
- Use pull requests for code review
- Keep commits focused and atomic
- Update documentation when making changes

## Performance
- Monitor bundle size and loading times
- Optimize images and assets
- Use proper lazy loading for components
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Monitor Core Web Vitals

## Deployment
- Test production builds locally before deployment
- Ensure all environment variables are properly configured
- Use proper build optimization settings
- Monitor application performance in production